                  text-transform: uppercase;
                "
              >
                Meanwhile</span
              >
            </td>
            <!-- Right flexible line -->
            <td
              valign="middle"
              style="
                width: 100%;
                font-size: 0;
                line-height: 0;
                padding: 0px;
                mso-line-height-rule: exactly;
              "
            >
              <div style="height: 0px; border-top: 4px solid #eeca66">
                &nbsp;
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </mj-table>
        <mj-image border-radius="10px" padding="10px 12px" width="600px" src="https://www.dubaisummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg" alt="REPLACE_ME" href="https://www.dubaisummary.com/" target="_blank" />
      
<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Vegas meets Yas
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Abu Dhabi will host the first Sphere venue outside the US, with Yas Island confirmed as its location. <a href="https://www.khaleejtimes.com/travel/uae-attractions/sphere-abu-dhabi-location-construction" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">Sphere Abu Dhabi</a> will be built between Yas Mall and SeaWorld Abu Dhabi, close to the island’s major attractions. The $1.7B venue is expected to be completed by the end of 2029 and will mirror the scale of Sphere Las Vegas, with capacity for up to 20,000 people. It will host immersive Sphere Experiences, concert residencies, brand events, sports, conferences, and product launches.</p>
</mj-text>

<mj-divider
  border-style="dashed"
  border-width="1px"
  border-color="lightgrey"
  padding="0px 12px 4px 12px"
/>

<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Flydubai schedule shakeup
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Flydubai has <a href="https://www.khaleejtimes.com/business/aviation/flydubai-says-it-has-revised-pakistan-flight-schedule-2" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">revised its flight schedule to Pakistan</a>, and affected passengers have been contacted directly about rebooking and refund options. As of May 13, bookings were unavailable for Islamabad, Lahore, and Peshawar until October 24-25, while flights to other Pakistani cities remained bookable. Flydubai said the changes follow reduced capacity linked to regional military conflict and warned passengers to confirm flight updates before travelling.</p>
</mj-text>

<mj-divider
  border-style="dashed"
  border-width="1px"
  border-color="lightgrey"
  padding="0px 12px 4px 12px"
/>

<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Tax waiver window
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">The UAE Federal Tax Authority says more than 91,000 taxable persons could benefit from its <a href="https://gulfnews.com/business/corporate-tax/uae-corporate-tax-penalty-waiver-may-benefit-91000-businesses-1.500540341" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">Corporate Tax Late Registration Penalty Waiver</a> initiative. More than 68,600 have already benefited, while over 22,000 remain eligible if they meet the conditions. The waiver applies to late corporate tax registration penalties incurred on or after June 1, 2023, and covers taxable persons and certain exempt persons who registered late.</p>
</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
